Modifications: the files were modified. SKILL.md was written fresh in the
house style with server-authority validation first; the references were
condensed into replication-and-rpc.md, join-and-disconnect.md,
sync-prediction.md and dedicated-server.md, GDScript first with C# attribute
forms. Facts were rechecked against the Godot 4.7 documentation (@rpc, Node,
MultiplayerSpawner, MultiplayerSynchronizer, SceneMultiplayer,
MultiplayerPeer, the high-level multiplayer tutorial, exporting for dedicated
servers). Fixes on port: the client spawn request that load()ed a
client-supplied path is replaced by a whitelisted spawner index;
set_multiplayer_authority is documented as local-only and set on every peer;
delta_interval and replication_interval 0.0 mean every network process
frame, not "disabled"; the nonexistent "headless" feature tag is removed in
favour of DisplayServer.get_name(); "Export as dedicated server" is described
as a resource export mode, not a separate template; "Linux/X11" is now
"Linux"; the snapshot interpolation uses a receive-time buffer instead of the
physics interpolation fraction; server arguments use OS.get_cmdline_user_args()
with documented precedence; C# server exports no longer claim the host needs
a .NET runtime; a protocol-version check, input clamping and lag-compensation
rewind limits were added; Dockerfile comments moved off instruction lines.
